re&gt;div]:border-border-400 [&amp;_.ignore-pre-bg&gt;div]:bg-transparent [&amp;_.standard-markdown_:is(p,blockquote,h1,h2,h3,h4,h5,h6)]:pl-2 [&amp;_.standard-markdown_:is(p,blockquote,ul,ol,h1,h2,h3,h4,h5,h6)]:pr-8 [&amp;_.progressive-markdown_:is(p,blockquote,h1,h2,h3,h4,h5,h6)]:pl-2 [&amp;_.progressive-markdown_:is(p,blockquote,ul,ol,h1,h2,h3,h4,h5,h6)]:pr-8"><div><div class="standard-markdown grid-cols-1 grid [&amp;_&gt;_*]:min-w-0 gap-3 standard-markdown"><p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]">Great question. Let me give you the full picture first, then the step-by-step guides.</p>
<hr class="border-border-200 border-t-0.5 my-3 mx-1.5">
<h3 class="text-text-100 mt-3 -mb-1 text-[1.125rem] font-bold">What's Left — Honest Checklist</h3>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]">Based on your professor's brief, here's everything remaining:</p>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]"><strong>✅ Done:</strong></p>
<ul class="[li_&amp;]:mb-0 [li_&amp;]:mt-1 [li_&amp;]:gap-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-disc flex flex-col gap-1 pl-8 mb-3">
<li class="whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Frontend code (React, all pages, homepage, combined requests, back button)</li>
<li class="whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Backend code (Node/Express, all APIs, middleware, auth)</li>
<li class="whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Database design (MongoDB schemas)</li>
<li class="whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Documentation (Word doc)</li>
</ul>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]"><strong>🔲 Still needed:</strong></p>
<ol class="[li_&amp;]:mb-0 [li_&amp;]:mt-1 [li_&amp;]:gap-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-decimal flex flex-col gap-1 pl-8 mb-3">
<li class="whitespace-normal break-words pl-2"><strong>GitHub</strong> — upload code</li>
<li class="whitespace-normal break-words pl-2"><strong>Deploy frontend</strong> — Vercel link</li>
<li class="whitespace-normal break-words pl-2"><strong>Deploy backend</strong> — Render link (you need this too, not just Vercel)</li>
<li class="whitespace-normal break-words pl-2"><strong>Deploy database</strong> — MongoDB Atlas (cloud DB, not localhost)</li>
<li class="whitespace-normal break-words pl-2"><strong>Postman/Thunder Client screenshots</strong> — test all APIs and save screenshots as evidence</li>
<li class="whitespace-normal break-words pl-2"><strong>MongoDB Atlas screenshots</strong> — showing your collections with real data</li>
<li class="whitespace-normal break-words pl-2"><strong>Handwritten documentation</strong> — the Word doc is your reference, but you still need to physically write/draw it by hand (professor is strict about this)</li>
<li class="whitespace-normal break-words pl-2"><strong>Individual contribution sheet</strong> — handwritten, one per member</li>
</ol>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]">The deployment is actually <strong>three separate things</strong> — frontend, backend, and database. Many students lose marks by only deploying the frontend and leaving the backend on localhost.</p>
<hr class="border-border-200 border-t-0.5 my-3 mx-1.5">
<h3 class="text-text-100 mt-3 -mb-1 text-[1.125rem] font-bold">Step 1 — GitHub (do this first, before deploying)</h3>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]"><strong>1.1 Create a GitHub account</strong> if you don't have one at github.com</p>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]"><strong>1.2 Create a new repository</strong></p>
<ul class="[li_&amp;]:mb-0 [li_&amp;]:mt-1 [li_&amp;]:gap-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-disc flex flex-col gap-1 pl-8 mb-3">
<li class="whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Click the <strong>+</strong> icon → New repository</li>
<li class="whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Name it: <code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">medstock</code></li>
<li class="whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Set to <strong>Public</strong></li>
<li class="whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Do NOT tick "Add README" (you already have one)</li>
<li class="whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Click <strong>Create repository</strong></li>
</ul>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]"><strong>1.3 Open terminal inside your project folder</strong></p>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]">Your project has two separate folders. You have two options — one repo with both, or two separate repos. One repo is cleaner:</p>
<div role="group" aria-label="Code" tabindex="0" class="relative group/copy bg-bg-000/50 border-0.5 border-border-400 rounded-lg focus:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-accent-100"><div class="sticky opacity-0 group-hover/copy:opacity-100 group-focus-within/copy:opacity-100 top-2 py-2 h-12 w-0 float-right"><div class="absolute right-0 h-8 px-2 items-center inline-flex z-10"><button class="inline-flex
