n><span>version</span></span></code></pre></div></div>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]">If it says "not recognized", download Git from <strong>git-scm.com</strong> → install with all default options → restart PowerShell after installing.</p>
<hr class="border-border-200 border-t-0.5 my-3 mx-1.5">
<h4 class="text-text-100 mt-2 -mb-1 text-base font-bold">Step 4 — Create GitHub repo</h4>
<ol class="[li_&amp;]:mb-0 [li_&amp;]:mt-1 [li_&amp;]:gap-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-decimal flex flex-col gap-1 pl-8 mb-3">
<li class="whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Go to <strong>github.com</strong> → sign in</li>
<li class="whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Click <strong>+</strong> (top right) → <strong>New repository</strong></li>
<li class="whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Name: <code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">medstock</code></li>
<li class="whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Set to <strong>Public</strong></li>
<li class="whitespace-normal break-words pl-2"><strong>Do NOT</strong> tick any checkboxes (no README, no .gitignore)</li>
<li class="whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Click <strong>Create repository</strong></li>
<li class="whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Copy the URL shown — it will look like:
<code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">https://github.com/YourUsername/medstock.git</code></li>
</ol>
<hr class="border-border-200 border-t-0.5 my-3 mx-1.5">
